        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for\noral argument before the Supreme Court of the\nUnited States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and\nmay it please the Court:\nWhen Coach Kennedy took a knee at\nmidfield after games to say a brief prayer of\nthanks, his expression was entirely his own.\nThat private religious expression was doubly\nprotected by the Free Exercise and Free Speech\nClauses.\nWhen the School District fired him for\nthat fleeting religious exercise out of\nendorsement concerns, it not only violated\nthe First Amendment, but it -- it ignored a\nveritable wall of this Court's precedents that\nmake clear that a school does not endorse\nprivate religious speech just because it fails\nto censor it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "change the subject, the record is clear that\nCoach Kennedy was fired for that midfield\nprayer, not for any earlier practices. And the\nrecord is equally clear that the District's sole\nreason for its actions was out of endorsement\nconcerns, not concerns for band members' safety\nor how many players joined the coach in the\nprayer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Clement, just so\nI'm clear, are you pursuing -- below, you had a\nfree exercise claim and you had a free speech\nclaim. Which are you pursuing? Are you\npursuing both now, or are you pursuing them\nseparately, or is this a -- sort of a hybrid\nclaim argument you're making?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Clement, I --\nI -- I have been trying to parse this out in a\nsimilar way to Justice Thomas, but let me just\ngive you a certain number of hypotheticals, and\ntell me what's -- when it becomes private and\nwhen it's still public."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So that is a neutral rule as you're explaining it to me. I think that's important to my answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- can I --\nCHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: -- Mr.\nClement, what if the -- the activity on the\nfield did not consist of this kneeling down\nbriefly but something more extensive, standing\nup on the 50-yard line, you know, arms\noutstretched, engaging in audible prayer?\nIs -- is your analysis and answer\nstill the same?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But would Pickering\napply, Mr. Clement, if, in the Chief Justice's\nhypothetical, let's say he says the Our Father\nwith arms outstretched and it starts causing a\nlot of havoc in the stands, a lot of the things\nthat, you know, your opponents, your friends on\nthe other side say that happened, that, you\nknow, the band members were being rushed, the\nhead coach feared for his life.\nIf his prayer of the Our Father caused\nthat kind of chaos, would Pickering apply, if\nthey said for reasons of efficiency and school\nsafety we just can't have this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: One of my problems in\nthis case was the parties seem to have different\nviews of the facts, so I'd like to get the --\nthis may be a case about facts and not really\nmuch about law, and that's why I wanted to try\nthis.\nI'll list six facts that I got out of\nthe record, and just tell me if they're right or\nwrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "no student joined him on the field on October 23, even though that's one of two specific incidents for which he was disciplined, that no players joined him on the 26th, which is the other game where he was"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I -- I take it from your earlier answers that you're not contesting the right of the School District to discipline Coach Kennedy if he had been praying during the official, if you will, post-game talk?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Coach Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you look at their first letter after the October 16th game, Joint Appendix page 90 to 95, there are eight references to endorsement or endorsing, zero references to either coercion or player safety."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "contemporaneously, when they put out a newsletter to their -- their constituents, they said there's no evidence that any student was coerced here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Okay. And then, to pick up on Justice Gorsuch, the Lemon endorsement test, that has not been applied by this Court in several decades in cases like Van Orden, Town of Greece, American Legion. At least I've said I don't think there is such a test in our case law anymore, the Lemon endorsement test, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: So Santa Fe is readily distinguishable. It is an endorsement case. So you might want to be clear that at least to that extent, it's no longer good law, but, here -- it's distinguishable. The loudspeaker is a huge part of it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And -- and, also, there's -- just to pick up on Justice Kagan's point, then you have the captive audience that seems to be at the heart of Engel, Lee versus Weisman, and Santa Fe, and the question really is, what's different here? You can answer that in any way you want, but just --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: How is that government speech? Would you explain that to me?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katskee",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATSKEE: Sure. In -- in Garcetti, this Court made clear that the test for government speech is a functional test, not a formalistic one, to determine whether the speech is pursuant to one's job."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that a violation of the -- can he be fired for engaging in those activities?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "School District",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We look at the employer's reason for the action that was taken. And if the reason that is given is an unlawful reason, then the employee wins."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why would Pickering apply? Have we ever applied Pickering just to straight-up free exercise claims?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "he was put on paid leave."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you have fired him?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What reason is there to believe that you would have treated that case the same way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can a school district take adverse action against a coach or a teacher because the coach or the teacher, on purely private time, not on school premises, not when the coach or teacher is discharging any official duties, is very, very visibly religious, posts all sorts of religious messages on YouTube?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0003-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can they -- can the district do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0004-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 98,
        "start": 98
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is Lemon in this\ncase? I mean, do we have to decide Lemon? The\nreason I ask, honestly, is because, if you see\nLemon, despite its imperfections, as an effort\nto take from other cases, and the first part of\nthe First Amendment, establishment is there\nfirst, an effort to prevent the country from"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul D. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0005-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, in terms of the correct test, I don't think the correct test when the government explicitly discriminates on the basis of religion is Pickering. Religion is different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul D. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The only thing worse than Pickering, I suppose, would be a center of attention test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul D. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0005-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, in terms of Santa Fe, we've discussed this a bunch, but my friend on the other side does say, well, wait, this is worse, this is coach speech, not student speech. But you can't strip away all the context of Santa Fe."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul D. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0005-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 111,
        "start": 111
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It uses the phrase \"endorse and endorsing\" and raises endorsement concerns eight times. It talks about safety concerns zero times. It talks about coercion concerns zero times."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul D. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-418",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "60b0ec2fc2cd3baf29016a6fd43c9c6eb91da23c4350d84cba1a1167c1811db4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60b0ec2fc2cd-0005-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 113,
        "start": 113
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Please do not remand to the Ninth Circuit for an application of the coercion test. There's no evidence of coercion contemporaneously."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
